WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.410
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.000
The KC Grand Prix has finally begun!

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.320
No matter who the opponent, I'm gonna win!

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.660
My first opponent is Mask the Rock.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.960
I don't know what kind of deck he uses.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.020
But I'll defeat him quick and remove his mask!

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.490
His tiny moves are so annoying!

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:57.170
What's that temple?

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.600
The Illusory Ancient Dragon

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.960
My turn!  I draw!

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:17.080
I summon Goblin Attack Force in attack position!

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.140
Goblin Attack Force attacks Ancient Giant!

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.400
I flip over my set card!

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.500
The Continuous Trap, Ordeal of a Traveler!

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.500
It activates when your monster attacks.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.450
You must select a card in my hand and guess what type it is.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:43.110
If you're wrong, your attacking monster returns to your hand.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.560
I only have one card in my hand.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.550
Guess what it is, Jonouchi!

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:52.650
Well?

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.020
Jonouchi is thinking hard.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:03.690
Because he lost to Sugoroku in their dice battle.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:08.700
Is it a spell?  Or a trap?  Or a monster?

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.580
I don’t know!  There's no way I can know!

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.800
Hurry up!

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.070
Be quiet!  It's a spell!

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.570
I say it’s a spell card!

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.180
Wrong!  Here’s the right answer.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.620
It's a monster.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.170
You rely on luck, but your luck’s run out!

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.570
It's not luck!  It's skill!

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:38.890
Skill?  He doesn't know what he's talking about.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:43.570
This is bad.  Jonouchi no longer has any monsters on his field.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:47.130
If Sugoroku attacks him directly next turn...

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.510
Jonouchi!

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.380
I set one card and end my turn!

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.720
My turn!  I draw!

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.380
Here I go, Jonouchi!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.830
Ancient Giant attacks you directly!

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.020
Go, Ancient Giant!

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.890
Giant Smash!

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:08.640
I flip over my set card, Scapegoat!

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.600
Don't underestimate me!

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.500
This duelist doesn't only rely on luck!

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.520
Then guess correctly using your brain.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:23.690
What?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.410
Ordeal of a Traveler is a Continuous Trap.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.120
So each time you attack, you must pass my quiz.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.730
F-Fine!

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:37.130
If I think carefully, I can figure out your hand!

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.130
One of them is Sinister Serpent.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:46.000
If I can figure out the other one, my monster can attack next turn.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.640
From my hand, I activate the Continuous Spell, Ancient Tome!

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.250
Nice!  This means his remaining card is Sinister Serpent.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:09.500
Ancient Tome allows me to swap one card in my hand with the top card in my deck.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.330
How dare you do that!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.760
Too bad, Jonouchi.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:20.370
I switch my two Stone Giant Tokens to defense position and end my turn.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:37.120
If Stone Giant Token doesn't attack, he takes 500 points of damage from each one.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.560
Why's he willing to lose life points to switch them to defense?

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.000
Damn!

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.000
My turn!  I draw!

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:49.110
Do I use Goblin Attack Force to attack again?

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:57.440
But if I guess wrong, I'll only have three Scapegoats on my field.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.290
If he draws a monster card next turn, I’ll lose.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.880
But I know it'll be Sinister Serpent!

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.420
I summon Goblin Attack Force in attack position!

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:15.640
What will you do now?

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.010
I end my turn!

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.100
Coward!

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.630
Jonouchi’s playing into Sugoroku's pace.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:28.320
It's so one-sided that I feel sorry for him.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.570
Professor Hopkins?

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.500
Grandpa...

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.160
Calling it at 10:53.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:52.160
Leon Wilson is the winner!

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.630
Get well, Doctor!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.860
We finally made it.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.530
It’s no dream or illusion!

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:20.790
It's really Kaiba Land!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:25.410
After coming this far, we have to enter this tournament!

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:30.320
You're right!  And finally crush Yugi and Jonouchi!

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:35.740
After forsaking our pride and honor, we have nothing to be scared of!

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.610
My turn!  I draw!

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:47.550
To keep Ancient Tome, I send one card in my hand to the graveyard.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:51.990
By sending Sinister Serpent to the graveyard, its effect activates.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:58.470
When it's in my graveyard during my Standby Phase, I can return it to my hand.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.930
Sinister Serpent, c'mon!

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.280
Are you messing with me?

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.060
No, Jonouchi.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:09.300
I'm done teasing you.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.410
What do you mean?

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:18.000
While you were losing your temper, I was quietly searching for treasure.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.250
Huh?  Search for treasure?

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:28.190
Yes!  My treasure is the legendary dragon sleeping inside Ancient City!

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.360
What are you talking about?

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:33.290
My other self?

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:39.620
When Ancient City's sacred door open, Ancient Dragon will resurrect.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:43.170
I now have the keys to open the door!

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:45.400
So that’s what he was going for!

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:51.510
I switch two Stone Giant Tokens from defense to attack position!

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:57.830
Switching Stone Giant Tokens' positions is the code to solving the puzzle!

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:02.480
I activate the Continuous Spell, Ancient Key on my field!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:13.100
I tribute Ancient Key and my Ancient Giant Tokens that changed from attack-defense-attack.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:18.710
That lets me play Ancient Gate from my deck, hand or graveyard.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.110
What’s this?

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:32.490
The Field Spell, Ancient City’s effect activates.

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:37.760
When Ancient Gate, Ancient Giant and Ancient Tome are all on the field...

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:45.320
...I can tribute them to resurrect the golden Ancient Dragon from its ancient sleep!

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:08.760
That's...

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.750
That's Sugoroku’s treasure.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.200
Grandpa…

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.230
Surprised, Jonouchi?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:24.530
Sugoroku actually found Ancient Dragon.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.840
What’s that?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:40.790
Ancient Gate, Ancient Key, Ancient Tome, Ancient Giant and two Stone Giant Tokens.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:44.320
You can't summon Ancient Dragon if even one was missing.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.720
It's a hard-to-find card, like ancient treasure.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:55.720
I've also been searching for these cards for years, as if I was racing Sugoroku.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:11:00.460
But I couldn't acquire the final card - Ancient Gate.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.850
But Sugoroku...

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:06.720
Hello?  It’s me, Arthur.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:13.720
Don't be shocked, but I finally found Ancient Gate!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.270
What?

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:18.670
Now I have all the cards!

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.130
Sugoroku…

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.260
Want to see it?

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:22.670
Of course.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:26.100
That's right!  That's why I’m going.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.670
To see how surprised they'll be!

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:33.530
Grandpa...

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:38.000
Yugi, that’s the type of guy Sugoroku is.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:42.840
He’s a top-class duelist, but he loves the cards themselves.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:46.480
He loves cards more than battling.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:52.000
So when he acquired that card, he wanted to show everyone.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.860
On the greatest stage.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.590
He's still like a kid.

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:57.300
Yeah.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.360
Nothing wrong with that.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:04.770
In a game of Duel Monsters, we should all act like children.

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:08.430
Sugoroku is fully enjoying this game.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:11.120
Enjoy…  I see!

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:27.560
What do you think of my treasure, Jonouchi?

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.240
Incredible, right?

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.800
That was a lot of work to bring out a single dragon!

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.170
I'd never build a deck like that!

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:40.100
Jonouchi, you've become boring.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:45.170
I'll show you how strong my treasure is!

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:49.290
Ancient Dragon attacks Goblin Attack Force!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.400
Go, Ancient Dragon!

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.880
Golden Bomber!

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:59.090
What?  Even my Sheep Tokens?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:02.840
Ancient Dragon’s effect activated.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.280
When it destroys your monster in battle...

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:09.700
...all your monsters in defense position are also destroyed.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.540
Damn!

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.930
This can't be real.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:23.010
I can’t lose to a masked freak!

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.970
I need to duel Yugi again!

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:29.220
Yugi?

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:32.220
Enjoy your duel, Jonouchi.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:37.240
You’re the one dueling, so have more fun!

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.610
But I…

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:42.610
You're not acting like yourself, Jonouchi!

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:46.680
Who cares if you win or lose this tournament?

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.210
Hey Honda, don't say that!

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:51.860
Jonouchi!  Just be yourself!

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:53.000
Jonouchi!

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.100
Everyone...

00:13:56.840 --> 00:14:01.000
Yugi, everyone...  You're so nice.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.840
Why are you crying?

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:07.650
Enjoy it, huh?

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:12.230
That’s right.  I'll just go all out in this duel!

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.320
That’s the spirit, Jonouchi!

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:17.160
Have fun!  And I will too!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:19.770
Good luck, Mask the Rock!

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.260
Why him?

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.880
Okay!

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:27.310
Here I go, you masked freak!

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:28.740
Bring it on!

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:31.410
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:38.220
I activate the spell card, Roll of Fate from my hand!

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:46.480
I draw cards from my deck equal to the number I roll.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:50.100
And I remove the same amount from my deck.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:56.150
I’ll use my Continuous Trap, The Legendary Gambler!

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.810
I rolled a 4!

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:03.180
And the masked freak rolled a 3!

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.000
All right!  I can activate Roll of Fate!

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:11.120
I'm getting excited!

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:13.050
W-What?

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:18.500
I activate the spell card, Landstar Forces from my hand!

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:26.930
It lets me Special Summon Level 3 and lower Landstars from my hand in attack position.

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:38.540
I Special Summon Brigadier of Landstar, Knight of Landstar and Grappler of Landstar in attack position!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:46.330
I tribute these three Landstars to Special Summon Gilford the Lightning in attack position!

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:51.880
Its effect activates!  Lightning Thunder!

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.460
What?

00:15:54.460 --> 00:16:03.000
When I tribute three monsters to summon it, all monsters on your field are destroyed.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:08.280
Ancient Dragon was…

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.910
There's more, you masked freak!

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:13.210
Gilford the Lightning attacks!

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:16.040
Then guess this card.

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:19.490
Too bad.  I know what it is this time.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:21.590
It's a monster card.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:24.220
A slithering snake.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:26.040
Well done.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:31.770
Gilford the Lightning, attacks him directly!

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:33.870
Lighting Crush Sword!

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.440
I end my turn.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:47.810
What?

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:50.960
The Field Spell, Ancient City’s effect activates.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:54.880
When it's on the field, if Ancient Dragon is destroyed...

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:59.190
...it's Special Summoned from the graveyard at the end of the turn.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:04.130
A dragon protected by this sacred shrine will never perish.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:07.070
How interesting!  That's the spirit!

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:09.320
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:14.040
Ancient Dragon attacks Gilford the Lightning!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.940
They both have 2800 attack points.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:19.820
They'll destroy each other!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:22.310
But that dragon…

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.150
Golden Bomber!

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:34.070
Gilford the Lightning…

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.870
I end my turn.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:51.070
This is fun.  This is why duels are exciting.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:54.010
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:59.830
I activate Pot of Greed from my hand!

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:03.060
I draw two cards from my deck!

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:15.540
Giant Trunade returns all spell and trap cards on the field to our hands.

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:20.260
If I use this to return Ancient City to his hand…

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:23.840
Premature Burial...

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:27.420
Wait a sec.  If I use Giant Trunade, my cards will also…

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:30.910
Jonouchi, this isn’t like you!

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:33.740
Stop thinking and just be lucky!

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:36.020
Be quiet!

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:39.540
You masked freak-  I mean, Mask the Rock!

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:48.330
I'm trying to think of what cards and combos to play, even though I'm not that smart.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.110
But it's really fun!

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.040
Jonouchi...

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:57.090
This is how I felt when I first started dueling.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:00.250
I'd forgotten this feeling.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:02.980
But I’m going to win!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:04.420
Here I go!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:10.710
I activate the Equip Spell, Premature Burial from my hand!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:17.620
By paying 800 life points, I'll bring back a monster from my graveyard in attack position!

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:20.270
Resurrect, Goblin Attack Force!

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:24.710
I activate the spell card, Giant Trunade from my hand!

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:28.810
What?

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:35.380
Giant Trunade’s effect returns all spell and trap cards to our hands.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.630
My shrine...

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:52.400
I see!  Ancient Dragon can't resurrect without that shrine!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:55.010
That’s not my only goal!

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:58.950
Premature Burial returned to my hand, so I activate it again!

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:00.150
What?

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:04.040
I Special Summon Gilford the Lightning from my graveyard!

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:09.950
Gilford the Lightning attacks Ancient Dragon!

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:13.350
Lightning Crush Sword!

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:22.000
What?

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:27.440
And Goblin Attack Force attacks you directly!

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:32.860
Jonouchi…

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:35.820
Used his brains to win!

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:42.160
That was a fun duel, you masked freak.

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:45.980
You’ve come a long way.

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:48.480
Jonouchi.

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.160
Sugoroku?

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:55.000
Everyone surprised?  It’s me - Sugoroku!

00:20:57.190 --> 00:21:02.000
You're tricky, Gramps!  I didn’t realize it was you!

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:03.720
Of course not!

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:06.490
Why are you here?

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.670
I came to meet you, Jonouchi.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:10.480
Me?

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:16.430
As your master, I felt I needed to watch one of your duels.

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:19.360
So how was my dueling?

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:25.290
Hmm...  Since you're having fun dueling, you've passed!

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:28.620
All right!  I passed!

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:31.200
What did he pass?

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.640
I’m getting a headache.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:39.640
I'm even more confused why your grandpa came here.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.640
You know why, right partner?

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:46.080
Of course.  To have the most fun.

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:08.990
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:17.360
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:19.090 --> 00:22:28.520
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:38.010
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:47.070
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:52.580
I'll live feeling them

00:22:53.190 --> 00:22:57.730
For me to be me

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:06.220
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:11.860
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:12.380 --> 00:23:21.520
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:26.770 --> 00:23:32.430
In the first match, Jonouchi defeated Mask the Rock aka Sugoroku.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:38.290
But I can't believe Jonouchi didn't know Sugoroku's identity until the end.

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:40.940
The next match is about to begin!

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:44.430
It's Rebecca's turn.  We have to go cheer for her!

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:47.500
Her opponent is... Vivian Wong?

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:50.040
Oh!  That weird girl!

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:53.660
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Fierce Fight!
Rebecca vs Vivian

00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:55.170
Duel, standby!
